{'symbol': 'REGN', 'date': '2021-09-14 17:33:00', 'title': 'REGENERON ANNOUNCES NEW U.S. GOVERNMENT AGREEMENT TO PURCHASE ADDITIONAL DOSES OF REGEN-COV™ (CASIRIVIMAB AND IMDEVIMAB) ANTIBODY COCKTAIL', 'text': 'TARRYTOWN, N.Y., SEPT. 14, 2021 /PRNEWSWIRE/ -- NEW AGREEMENT FOR 1.4 MILLION DOSES OF REGEN-COV, BRINGS TOTAL PURCHASED BY THE U.S. GOVERNMENT TO NEARLY 3 MILLION DOSES REGEN-COV CURRENTLY AUTHORIZED TO TREAT CERTAIN INFECTED PATIENTS TO REDUCE RISK OF HOSPITALIZATION OR DEATH FROM COVID-19, AND FOR POST-EXPOSURE PROPHYLAXIS FOR CLOSE CONTACTS OF INFECTED INDIVIDUALS REGENERON\xa0PHARMACEUTICALS, INC.\xa0(NASDAQ: REGN) TODAY\xa0ANNOUNCED THAT THE U.S. DEPARTMENT OF HEALTH AND HUMAN SERVICES (HHS) AND THE DEPARTMENT OF DEFENSE (DOD) WILL PURCHASE 1.4 MILLION ADDITIONAL DOSES OF REGEN-COV (CASIRIVIMAB AND IMDEVIMAB).'}